# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.env

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
*.claude

# PWA / Bubblewrap (TWA) — never commit signing keys or build output
*.keystore
*.jks
pwa/android/
pwa/app-release-*

# ─── Never commit reference/export docs or secret material ──────────
# Postman collections/environments routinely contain live access tokens,
# refresh tokens and plaintext passwords. See rules.llm.
*postman_collection*.json
*postman_environment*.json
postman/

# API specs, authentication walkthroughs, and implementation/reference docs.
/ALL_APIs.md
/AUTHENTICATION_LOGIN_FLOW.md
/*_GUIDE.md
/*_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

# Generic secret material (defence in depth).
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# ─── Local QA / E2E planning material ─────────────────────────────
# qa/ is the design spec for the Playwright suite: harness design, stub
# catalogue, per-module coverage. It is reference documentation (it maps
# internal routes, endpoints and permission codes), so rules.llm keeps it out
# of Git.
#
# The test CODE is different: rules.llm explicitly allows source and tests, so
# the suite lives in the committed e2e/ folder. Keep them apart — moving spec
# files into qa/ would make git silently drop them.
#
# e2e/.auth/ is separately ignored: it holds storageState files containing
# refresh tokens, and is regenerated by the Playwright setup project.
/qa/

# Playwright run artefacts (traces, screenshots, videos, reports) and
# generated auth state.
e2e/.auth/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
e2e-results.xml
